   "i": 26,
   "shape_h": "p",
   "shape_m": "p",
   "html_text": "One difficulty faced by such characterizations is that of making clear what the relevant facts are supposed to be. The difficulty is particularly acute in certain debates, for instance in the debate over tense realism. For what is it for a fact to be tensed? It cannot simply be said that a tensed fact is a fact that can be referred to by means of a tensed description of type “the fact that ⟦M⟧ ”, where “ ⟦M⟧ ” is a tensed sentence. For it is open to a B-theorist to hold that such expressions do ",
   "md_text": "One difficulty faced by such characterizations is that of making clear what the relevant facts are supposed to be. The difficulty is particularly acute in certain debates, for instance in the debate over tense realism. For what is it for a fact to be tensed? It cannot simply be said that a tensed fact is a fact that can be referred to by means of a tensed description of type “the fact that ⟦M⟧ ”, where “ ⟦M⟧ ” is a tensed sentence. For it is open to a B-theorist to hold that such expressions do "
